<div class="article-detail-page">
    <div class="article-body">
        <p>If your payment is declined on Lively, you can retry or update your payment method. Here's how to fix common problems with payments and where to check order & receipts.</p>
        <p>This article covers troubleshooting payments inside and outside a show. If you need help with Afterpay, check out <a href="#">Buy Now, Pay Later</a>.</p>

        <p><strong>On this page:</strong></p>
        <ul>
            <li><a href="#">Why payments decline</a></li>
            <li><a href="#">Fix a declined payment</a></li>
            <li><a href="#">Troubleshoot charges</a></li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Why payments decline</h2>
        <p>Payments can fail for a few reasons:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Not enough funds available</li>
            <li>Card expired or invalid</li>
            <li>Incorrect card details (number, expiration date, CVV security code, billing address)</li>
            <li>Bank flagged the payment for review</li>
        </ul>

        <p>If you've confirmed everything looks correct and your payment still won't go through, contact your bank. In the meantime, you can continue to checkout using a different payment option.</p>

        <h2>Fix a declined payment</h2>
        <p><strong>During a live show</strong></p>
        <p>When you bid on an item and your payment declines, you'll get an error notification that says:</p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Add new payment method:</strong> Your current card is invalid or has expired.</li>
            <li><strong>Retry payment:</strong> Your payment could not process.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Tap the warning notification to <a href="#">update your payment method</a>.</p>

        <p>The seller is also alerted when they go to list your item so they know the payment failed.</p>

        <h2>Troubleshoot charges</h2>
        <h3>Why was I charged USD 1.00?</h3>
        <p>When you add a payment method or first register, you may see a temporary authorization charge (usually USD 1.00). This helps confirm your account is valid and in good standing. This hold will drop from your bank statement within a few days.</p>

        <h3>Why am I seeing a recurring charge?</h3>
        <p>Lively doesn't offer subscriptions. If you see a recurring charge, it may be because:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>You used a Buy Now, Pay Later provider.</li>
            <li>Your banking account authorizes multiple identical purchases differently.</li>
        </ul>

